# 📖 TOEFL Reading - Day33

## Passage

Scientists have long studied how ecosystems maintain stability despite changes in their environments. One important factor is biodiversity, which refers to the variety of living organisms in an ecosystem. Researchers have obtained evidence suggesting that ecosystems with greater biodiversity may be better able to recover from environmental disturbances. For example, if one species declines because of a change in temperature, other species may continue performing similar ecological functions. Studies have also revealed that ecosystems with lower biodiversity can sometimes be more vulnerable to sudden changes.

---

## Question 1

What is the main idea of the passage?

A. Biodiversity may help ecosystems maintain stability.

B. Ecosystems cannot recover from environmental changes.

C. Temperature is the only factor affecting ecosystems.

D. Scientists have stopped studying biodiversity.

Answer: A

---

## Question 2

What have researchers obtained evidence about?

A. The effects of biodiversity on ecosystem stability

B. The disappearance of all species

C. The causes of temperature changes

D. The history of scientific research

Answer: A

---

## Question 3

Why might an ecosystem with greater biodiversity recover more easily?

A. All species perform exactly the same function.

B. Other species may continue performing similar ecological functions.

C. Biodiversity prevents environmental changes.

D. Species cannot be affected by temperature.

Answer: B

---

## Question 4

What does "reveal" most likely mean?

A. Hide

B. Discover or show

C. Prevent

D. Maintain

Answer: B

